"g":"covering; sheath; holder (of anything)","t":163,"x":["Reperimus inter exempla Hermotimi Clazomenii animam relicto corpore errare solitam vagamque e longinquo multa adnuntiare, quae nisi a praesente nosci non possent, corpore interim semianimi, donec cremato eo inimici, qui Cantharidae vocabantur, remeanti animae veluti vaginam ademerint; […]","Omnia quidem principalia viscera membranis propriis ac velut vaginis inclusit providens natura; […]"]},{"g":"covering; sheath; holder (of anything)","t":163},{"g":"covering; sheath; holder (of anything)","t":245,"x":["Noctu in vigiliam quando ibat miles, quom tu ibas simul,","Ex hac igitur Scandza insula quasi officina gentium aut certe velut vagina nationum cum rege suo nomine Berig Gothi quondam memorantur egressi: qui ut primum e navibus exientes terras attigerunt, ilico nomen loci dederunt."]},{"g":"covering; sheath; holder (of anything)","t":246,"x":["Mirum pardos, pantheras, leones et similia condito in corporis vaginas unguium mucrone, ne refringantur hebetenturve, ingredi aversisque falculis currere nec nisi in adpetendo protendere."]}],"f":[["vāgīna",212],["vāgīnae",2],["vāgīna",7,3],["vāgīnae",14,3],["vāgīnae",3,3],["vāgīnārum",13,3],["vāgīnae",6,3],["vāgīnīs",12,3],["vāgīnam",5,3],["vāgīnās",11,3],["vāgīnā",4,3],["vāgīnīs",10,3],["vāgīna",8,3],["vāgīnae",15,3]],"tpl":["la-ndecl"],"ipa":[{"i":"[waːˈɡiː.na]","t":0},{"i":"[vaˈd͡ʒiː.na]","t":1},{"i":"[waːˈɡiː.naː]","t":0}],"ety":{"text":"From Proto-Italic *wāgīnā (“sheath, scabbard”), possibly from Proto-Indo-European *wag- (“sheath, cover”). Tentatively cognate with Lithuanian vóžti (“to cover”).","tpl":[{"k":52,"lang":56,"form":"*wāgīnā","gloss":"sheath, scabbard"},{"k":52,"lang":48,"form":"*wag-","gloss":"sheath, cover"},{"k":42,"lang":"lt","form":"vóžti","gloss":"to cover"}]},"rel":{"d":["ēvāgīnō","neovāgīna","vāgīna dentāta","vāgīnālis","vāgīnārius","vāgīnātor","vāgīnātus","vāgīnella","vāgīnula"],"r":["ēvāgīnātiō"],"syn":["cunnus"]}}],"vicecomes":[{"w":"viceco